Module ombra "The Book of Faces" {
  // ── When the book closes ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // At midnight on the ninth night, or when the Concord's offer of a face has been answered after a Drawing has been held.
  // The first whose condition holds wins, in the order written. What became of each of the city's people is told in the
  // hour before (aftermath.kyr). In a world that goes on, Ombra goes on after it.
  Rule drawing_over when closing() and not drawingOver(ombra_delta) { Assert drawingOver(ombra_delta). }

  // The Concord's offer: the last act. A face, or the road home with the Concord's thanks.
  Kind white_domino_kind "the Warrant's white domino" is gear worth 0 weighing 0 granting insight described "A plain white half-mask of the kind a Registrar wears, with the bare oval of the Concord stamped on the inside of the brow, and no name on it anywhere. A Fitter has cut it to your face from a cast you never sat for, and it fits like a thing you were born holding. By day in Ombra it is answered as a person. It gives away nothing at all, which is its whole use.".
  Item white_domino "the Warrant's white domino" is white_domino_kind at offstage.
  Kind countersigned_warrant_kind "the Stranger's Warrant, countersigned" is gear worth 0 weighing 0 granting persuasion described "The grey slip you were given on the first morning, with a second oval stamped over the first in the Chaplain's violet and a line in a small round hand: THE CONCORD THANKS THE BARE, AND DOES NOT ASK THEM TO STAY. Anywhere the Concord's name is known, it is a passport; and anywhere it is not, a very well-bred piece of paper.".
  Item countersigned_warrant "the Stranger's Warrant, countersigned" is countersigned_warrant_kind at offstage.
  Action accept_face(actor: group, who: member, site: place) "Accept the face the Concord offers, and let {who} wear it" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, urn_hall) and drawingHeld(actor) and warrantHeld(actor) and not faceTaken(actor) and not faceDeclined(actor) and awake(who) and memberOf(who, actor).
    Time 5.
    Resolve endow(who, wisdom, by_one).
    On success { Assert faceTaken(actor). Assert holdsFace(actor, face_white). Give white_domino to actor. }
    Result "Sergeant Vail finds you at the foot of the dais. She has the grey slip in her glove. 'A face,' she says. 'Your own. A trade, a place in the next Urn, a name nobody may say, and nobody will.' There is a question in how she is standing. You take it. She puts into your hands a white half-mask the plain size of a person; it fits, and the whole room, which has not been able to look at you for nine days, looks at you as at one of itself. You will be, in Ombra, from now on, a person. You find you did not know until this minute how much you wanted it, or what it would cost.".
  }
  Action decline_face(actor: group, who: member, site: place) "Decline the face, and go home Bare" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, urn_hall) and drawingHeld(actor) and warrantHeld(actor) and not faceTaken(actor) and not faceDeclined(actor) and awake(who) and memberOf(who, actor).
    Time 5.
    Resolve endow(who, charisma, by_one).
    On success { Assert faceDeclined(actor). Give countersigned_warrant to actor. Increase quantity(actor, gold) by 100. }
    Result "'Bare,' says the Watch, and then, after a time, in a voice she has not used all week, 'You are the second to refuse it in sixty-two years.' She does not seem surprised. She hands you the Warrant, stamped a second time, and a purse of a hundred coin in the Concord's grey leather, and says the thing the Concord says to its Bare, and which you are fairly sure she has just made up: 'The city thanks you, and does not ask you to stay.' Then she puts her mask straight and, more quietly: 'I should have asked.'".
  }
  Action vail_joins(actor: group, site: place) "Ask Sergeant Vail whether she would walk out of Ombra with you, some day" {
    Speaker vail.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(vail, site) and vailTrust(actor) >= 3 and (faceTaken(actor) or faceDeclined(actor)) and not vailWilling(actor).
    Time 5.
    On success { Assert vailWilling(actor). Assert willing(vail, actor). Set hire(vail) to 0. }
    Result "'I have been a hound for nineteen years,' says Ottoline Vail. She takes the black domino off and looks at it in her hand, in the Urn Hall, in front of the Watch. 'I find that I am prepared to be a person for a little while, on the road, where nobody is anybody and it is allowed.' She hangs it on the Urn's wax. 'Ask me again when I have got used to it. I will say yes.'".
  }
  Relation vailWilling(group).

  // Each ending is the Drawing's way, said as the city has it in the morning.
  Ending end_put_out "Put Out at the Gate" when gateShut(party) "By the sixth mark the Watch has stopped being patient and started being procedure. The Warrant is struck through with a line of white wax and the Gate of Strangers is closed on you with a very small, very civil sound, like a ledger shutting. Behind you the Novena goes on in its rain. You do not hear who is drawn. You hear, from a long way down the delta road, on the ninth night, a crowd breathing out, and cannot tell if it is relief.".
  Ending end_quiet_hand "The Quiet Hand" when closing() and wayQuiet(party) "Ombra goes to bed on the ninth night as it has done every year for thirty-one, and wakes to a city with nineteen new faces in it, none of whom knows how they came there. The Urn is sealed again. The Book is back on its lectern. A woman in a white mask is read the lots at the next Drawing, and the next; she has your handwriting, and goes about the streets by night in the Registrar's mask, mending. It is, by every measure that Ombra has, a very well-governed city. Only you know why. On the ninth night you walk out along the delta road with the grey Warrant folded in your sleeve, and nobody asks for it back.".
  Ending end_open_book_consent "The Consenting Book" over end_open_book when closing() and wayOpenBook(party) and openBookConsent(party) "Fifty-one stood up. In the days after, a great many more, in doorways, in the bread-market, on the Chapel steps, a mask in their hand, saying: it was I. Orsolya Hart has stopped saying her own name as a crime and begun saying it as an introduction. The Spent begin to be spoken to. There are two duels and a marriage. The city, which had thought of the Concord as the thing that protected it from itself, finds it was the thing that stopped it from being brave. It does not become good. It becomes a little less safe, and a little more known; and nobody, for the moment, is Named who did not ask.".
  Ending end_open_book "The Open Book" when closing() and wayOpenBook(party) "By morning the names are in every square. The Treasurer of the Year of the Sluice is a lamp-trimmer's daughter, dead, and the city does not know whether to curse her or to bury her; it does both, in a quarrel that lasts nine days. The Candid hold the Chapel, and the Registry, and the Book, and a register of names on a board outside it, which is for the first time a thing in Ombra that can be asked for. By the end of the week, in the Drip, two old feuds have been restarted over the dead. There is a debt, in the Exchange, that has found its man. Absalom Peck, if he is living, is cheered in the street, which kills him faster than the Naming did.".
  Ending end_honest_urn "The Honest Urn" when closing() and wayHonest(party) "The first Office goes to a girl of seventeen who had come in out of the rain; the second, to a man who immediately sells it, which is not allowed, and is overturned at the Hearing. The Treasurer is a drunk. The Warden of Locks is a woman who has never locked a door. The Physician-General, by a margin of nine tesserae, is a person who is in every other respect a physician. It is, for a year, the worst-governed city on the delta, and the most alive, and in the Rains the Cullet Sluice holds, by an accident of chance, in the hands of a ferryman's son who has no idea what a sluice is and asks, and is told.".
  Ending end_qualified "The Qualified Draw" when closing() and wayQualified(party) "It is a civic compromise, and is called one by every faction, and satisfies none. The Offices go by lot out of those whom the city has already said it trusts. Anybody may put a name on the list. By the first Novena a ferrywoman is Treasurer, protesting; the Candid have nailed the list to the Chapel door and are correcting its spelling; and in the Drip they have started a column for it on the Tally-cloth, in chalk, with odds. It is a worse lottery than the Urn's, and a better government than the Registrar's, and neither the Candid nor the Old Names nor the Chapel have been able to find the principle on which to attack it, since it is, at bottom, what the Rounds were.".
  Ending end_nobody "The Year of Nobody" when closing() and wayNobody(party) "For a year there is no Treasurer, no Warden and no Serene in Ombra, and everybody knows who they are. The sluices are kept by the people who live below them; the Weights are kept by whoever happens to be holding the scale; the lamps are lit by the Owls and the bread weighed by the Cockles and the Watch walks about with its mask in its hand, asking for directions. It is chaos, in the sense that nobody is sure who is in charge, and a festival, in the sense that nobody minds. At the next Novena the Urn is brought out and there is a great deal of discussion as to whether to put anything in it. It is put to a show of hands. The hands do not agree.".
  Ending end_old_names "The Old Names Come Down" when closing() and wayOldNames(party) "The Fourteen come down from Quiet Hill in the morning, in daylight, in silk, with their shutters open. The Contessa Tarn is the first Registrar in three hundred years to read the Offices in her own name. It is not a tyranny. It is, if anything, a very stylish and exacting regime of the elderly, who have a great many opinions on the lamps and the weights. The Feud does not restart, because nobody is quite sure who would be the other side. The Seconds' Guild is paid. In the Drip they begin, after a month, to call their children after the Houses, which is how you know it has worked.".
  Ending end_stranger "The Stranger's Face" when closing() and wayStranger(party) "You are the Serene of Ombra, for a year, in white and gold, and nobody can say so. It is quiet in the Mask. There are things the Serene may not say and things the Serene may not hear, and in between a great deal of weather. At the end of the year there is a Drawing. You are drawn out of the Urn; you stand there, bare, in the Urn Hall, and they say, 'We do not know who you are,' which is, you find, a very great relief. A woman in a lamp-trimmer's grey says she will see you home. You are not at all sure that she is not the Registrar, and you do not ask.".
  Ending end_interregnum "The Interregnum" when closing() and not drawingHeld(party) "At the stroke of midnight the Concord's own text takes effect: all nineteen Offices dissolve, being only masks. There is a long silence in the Urn Hall in which everybody present looks at the faces next to them, and finds them to be a stranger's. Then the sluice-keepers go home, and the Watch lays down its hounds, and in the Drip somebody lights a lamp that nobody has told them to. For some days it is a city without a government. A ferryman is seen to ask a Watch domino the time, and to be told. By the Novena's end the Old Names have a hold on the Hill, the Candid on the Row and the Rain-Wives on the Drip, and the three of them are discussing, with a seriousness neither of them had planned for, the matter of a Concord.".
}
